---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import InquiryDialog from '../components/InquiryDialog.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/paths';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About TRAKNOVA | Industrial Mobility"
  description="TRAKNOVA is an industrial mobility partner for rugged PDA computers, RFID handhelds, industrial tablets, configuration and OEM / ODM cooperation."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="wrap">
        <span class="eyebrow">ABOUT TRAKNOVA</span>
        <h1>A partner for the work<br /><em>between the scan and the system.</em></h1>
        <p>TRAKNOVA builds and configures rugged mobile computers, RFID handhelds and industrial tablets for distributors, solution providers and enterprise teams. Our focus is the practical detail that decides whether a deployment works.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">WHAT WE DO</span><h2>Hardware, configuration<br />and a path to rollout.</h2></div>
          <p>We are not only a device supplier. We help define the capture method, select the platform, confirm the configuration and plan the support path.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quality-grid">
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Product platforms</h3>
            <p>Rugged PDA computers, RFID devices and industrial tablets for enterprise data capture.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Barcode and multifunction handhelds</li>
              <li>Short-range and UHF RFID</li>
              <li>Android and Windows rugged tablets</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Configuration &amp; branding</h3>
            <p>Platform options aligned to the application, market and brand.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Capture module selection</li>
              <li>Accessories and mounting</li>
              <li>OS image and preload</li>
              <li>Private label and packaging</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Deployment support</h3>
            <p>A practical plan for piloting, documenting and sustaining the fleet.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Workflow and exception mapping</li>
              <li>Pilot planning</li>
              <li>Documentation package</li>
              <li>Spares planning</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">HOW WE WORK</span><h2>Principles that survive<br />a real deployment.</h2></div>
          <p>These are the standards we apply to a single device order and to a multi-site rollout.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pillar-grid">
          <article class="pillar"><b>01</b><h3>Workflow first</h3><p>We start with the task and the exception, not with a device category.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar"><b>02</b><h3>Honest specifications</h3><p>Only confirmed values are published. Configuration details are confirmed against the approved datasheet.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar"><b>03</b><h3>Practical engineering</h3><p>Devices, modules and accessories are selected for the environment they will actually work in.</p></article>
          <article class="pillar"><b>04</b><h3>Support after rollout</h3><p>Spares, documentation and change notification are part of the plan, not an afterthought.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">CAPABILITY MAP</span><h2>What we can<br />cover for you.</h2></div>
          <p>Availability and scope are confirmed per product, platform and project. The map below shows where we typically work with partners.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="matrix-wrap">
          <table class="matrix-table series-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Capability</th><th>What it covers</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Product platforms</td><td>Rugged PDA, short-range and UHF RFID handhelds, Android and Windows industrial tablets</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Auto-ID</td><td>1D / 2D barcode, UHF and short-range RFID, NFC, ID / document capture</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Configuration</td><td>Capture modules, memory and OS variants, accessories, mounting</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Branding</td><td>Private label, boot animation, packaging, manuals, serialization</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Documentation</td><td>Datasheets, user manuals, quick guides, packaging artwork, test documentation</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Support</td><td>Pilot planning, staging, spares, after-sales coordination</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">QUALITY &amp; DOCUMENTATION</span><h2>Evidence before<br />assurances.</h2></div>
          <p>We do not publish certifications we cannot evidence. The applicable test plan, document package and market approvals are agreed per product and project.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="quality-grid">
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Incoming and in-process</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Incoming material checks</li>
              <li>Assembly and process checks</li>
              <li>Process records retained</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Final inspection</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Functional checks</li>
              <li>Packaging and label verification</li>
              <li>Test records retained per batch</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="quality-card">
            <h3>Documentation</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Datasheet and user manual</li>
              <li>Quick guide and packaging artwork</li>
              <li>Conformity documentation where available</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="note-line">Certifications, test reports and factory information are provided to qualified partners during due diligence.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="split-intro">
          <div><span class="eyebrow">WHO WE WORK WITH</span><h2>Different partners,<br />different depth.</h2></div>
          <p>Our cooperation model adapts to whether you distribute, integrate or operate the deployment.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="family-grid">
          <article class="family-card">
            <span class="family-count">DISTRIBUTORS</span>
            <h3>Range and brand</h3>
            <p>A product range, configuration support and OEM options for your market.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Product range and accessories</li>
              <li>Private label and packaging</li>
              <li>Regional documentation</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/oem-odm/')}>Explore OEM / ODM →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="family-card">
            <span class="family-count">SOLUTION PROVIDERS</span>
            <h3>Fit to the application</h3>
            <p>Devices and modules selected around the application, with pilot support.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Capture module selection</li>
              <li>Pilot planning</li>
              <li>Software and MDM integration</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/solutions/')}>Explore solutions →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="family-card">
            <span class="family-count">ENTERPRISE TEAMS</span>
            <h3>From review to rollout</h3>
            <p>A practical path from workflow review to device shortlist and fleet rollout.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Workflow review</li>
              <li>Device shortlist and configuration</li>
              <li>Rollout and spares planning</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/contact/')}>Talk to our team →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section-soft">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="special-grid">
          <article class="special-card">
            <span class="mini-label">COMPANY INFORMATION</span>
            <h3>Due diligence, without the theatre.</h3>
            <p>Registered entity details, manufacturing location, certifications and test reports are provided to qualified partners on request. We prefer to share evidence rather than unverifiable claims.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Registered company details</li>
              <li>Manufacturing and quality documentation</li>
              <li>Certification and test reports where applicable</li>
            </ul>
          </article>
          <article class="special-card">
            <span class="mini-label">TALK TO US</span>
            <h3>Start with your workflow.</h3>
            <p>Tell us the application, target market and expected volume. We will confirm the right platform and the information you need to evaluate it.</p>
            <div class="mt-36"><button class="button button-accent" data-inquiry-open>Send an Inquiry ↗</button></div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="wrap cta-band">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">HAVE A PROJECT TO DISCUSS?</span>
          <h2>Let's find the right<br />starting point.</h2>
          <p>Share the workflow, target market and volume. We will take it from there.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button button-accent" href={withBase('/contact/')}>Contact Our Team ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer /><InquiryDialog />
</BaseLayout>
